From c459233afbec2c9dca8c06cfce53809eb1a6c99c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:43:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 185/217] feat: ShadePass and the world-space light grid in
 CSvoRenderer (stage 2A, renderer)

The renderer half of hit shading. Everything is behind e_svoTI_RT_Active and
GetIntegratioMode() == 2; with the cvar off no target is allocated, no pass is
dispatched and DemosaicPass reads exactly the pair it read before.

- CheckAllocateRT: four extra specular-set targets - HITPOS (RGBA32F, because
  fp16 quantises to 1.5 cm at 32 m and that position is fed to the shadow
  cascades), RAYDIR (fp16), and an ALD/RGB pair for ShadePass to write, since it
  reads the tracing pair as g-data and cannot write it at the same time. They
  are released again when the cvar goes off.
- ConeTracePass binds the two g-data targets as MRT 2/3, and explicitly unbinds
  them otherwise so a member pass object cannot keep last frame's bindings while
  the shader has two outputs.
- BuildRTLightGridPass: a CGpuBuffer of dim^3 x 8 uints, dim = e_svoTI_RT_LightGridDim
  rounded to a multiple of 8, dispatched dim/8 per axis over a box of camera
  +- (e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistCam + e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay), reading the existing tiled
  light list. No new CPU-side light collection at all.
- ShadePass: the forward per-pass resource set filled from CSvoRenderer rather
  than borrowed from CSceneForwardStage, whose position in the frame relative to
  the SVO passes is not guaranteed. Sun cascades through the volumetric-fog
  precedent (SetupShadowsForFog + SetShadowCascadesToRenderPass +
  SetShadowSamplingContextToRenderPass), the tiled shade-info buffer, the
  projector and probe atlases, the shadow pool, the env BRDF LUT, the light grid
  at t33, and a CBPerPassForward (b5) filled from the same Fog / VolumetricFog /
  ShadowUtils / cloud / SVOGI sources SceneForward.cpp uses. Deliberately NOT
  called here: SetupSvoTexturesForRead and SetupRsmSunTextures, which would
  fight the forward set for t17-t20 and t26-t31.
- UpdateRender: TI_LIGHTGRID then TI_SHADE_SPEC, after the specular cone trace
  and before its de-mosaic.
- SVO_ShadeParams0.z (Neo's distance AO) is left at 0: it darkens by hit
  distance and double-counts against ApplyGI mode 0, which is also AO.

